  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the circuit shown in the figure (A), <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is a variable resistance. As the value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is changed, the current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> through the cell varies as shown in the figure (B). As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math>, the current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.&nbsp;What is the value of the sum of the resistances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in ohms?</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image13-ffe5fce5-9a5d-4187-8c6e-b13b67a5b75b.jpg\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 194px;\" /></p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> (from the graph).In this situation, the circuit can be drawn as shown in figure <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> .<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image14-5aa0c129-fced-4188-834c-15919b2db198.jpg\" /><br /><br />[current through R<sub>2&nbsp;</sub>will be zero because we have a short circuit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>]<br /><br />Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>&nbsp;</p>",
